INSERT OR IGNORE INTO entities (id, type, name, description, url, image_url, role, tagline, featured, see_also_json) VALUES ('entity-f7d77401', 'person', 'USA - NY', '"USA - NY" serves within the archive as a regional designation representing intactivist advocacy and educational outreach based in New York State, United States. Operating at the intersection of bodily integrity, medical ethics, and human rights, this entity has contributed to raising public awareness regarding the ethical and medical implications of non-therapeutic infant circumcision. Through localized grass-roots organizing, public demonstrations, and distribution of educational literature, the entity has represented a crucial node in the broader American genital autonomy movement.

Throughout its documented history in the archive, USA - NY engaged with medical professionals, parents, and legislators to challenge prevailing cultural norms surrounding routine neonatal circumcision. The entity''s efforts frequently focused on advocating for informed consent, highlighting the rights of the child to bodily integrity, and providing resources for intact care and foreskin restoration support within the state of New York.

By establishing a visible presence in a major media and population center, USA - NY played a significant role in expanding the reach of the intactivist message during key periods of public debate. Its contributions remain recorded in archival literature as an example of state-level organized opposition to routine infant circumcision in the United States.', '', '', 'champion', 'A regional intactivist initiative dedicated to promoting bodily autonomy and ending routine infant circumcision in New York State.', 1, '[{"name": "Two Creative Guys", "score": 11.116, "shared_docs": 4}, {"name": "Uncircumcised Society of America - New York", "score": 11.116, "shared_docs": 3}, {"name": "Ricky Carr", "score": 11.116, "shared_docs": 3}, {"name": "Tom", "score": 11.116, "shared_docs": 3}, {"name": "Gene", "score": 10.531, "shared_docs": 4}]');
